@kstatefb @carver_willis77 ‼️⬇️

@64amdg Review: “Excited to have @carver_willis77 out to the Center Summit. Carver has been a mainstay out in AZ with my @amdg_performance team since high school. Historically he has been an OT, and a very good one. However, with the demands of the Center position evolving, WHO can be successful at this position is more wide open than ever. This past draft we saw a LT get drafted in the 1st round to play Center, and a guy that played some DL while in college, before being converted to a full time C, win the @therimingtontrophy and get drafted in the 2nd round. 

A big, physical, smart, and athletic athlete that can bend like @carver_willis77 has the tools. The rest is desire and a willingness to wade through growing pains. But big picture, a player that can ONLY play Center better be damn near a HOF talent in order to stick on an NFL roster. Carver is adding another tool to his arsenal to give himself the best chance to carve out an NFL career, by exploring the possibilities of his growth. 💡#SnapUp #AMDG

